<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Germany</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Germany</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-ger</id><updated>2026-11-27T00:42:58Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-ger" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-1432?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-ger" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>On farewell trip, Steinmeier calls for more investment in Africa</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:72af0cfb9b525a2ac35d43146076b26bebeb42f8a5cef1c07f282a6138aaba99</id><updated>2026-11-27T00:42:16Z</updated><published>2026-11-26T17:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/on-farewell-trip-steinmeier-calls-for-more-investment-in-africa/a-80067717--a2b49bd3f417.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/on-farewell-trip-steinmeier-calls-for-more-investment-in-africa/a-80067717?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Cote d'Ivoire, Ghana, Kenya: On his last trip to Africa, outgoing German President Frank-Walter Steinmeier called on companies at home to be bolder and seize opportunities in Africa.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Trial of Berlin woman accused of spying for Russia begins after delay</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:379977ea21f46df5045d59230af7eb2f04f5adb5d850129a5f9c732319ce6c05</id><updated>2026-11-27T00:42:10Z</updated><published>2026-11-26T17:44:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/trial-of-berlin-woman-accused-of-spying-for-russia-begins-after-delay/a-80057677--743246431230.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/trial-of-berlin-woman-accused-of-spying-for-russia-begins-after-delay/a-80057677?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Despite delays due to health issues, the trial of the Berlin woman accused of spying for Russia has begun. Prosecutors say the defendant used her military contacts to provide information on German defense and Ukraine.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany: IG Metall union says deal reached with employers</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f79af0046ef19a5abe1fa59c8afa8129da204d580820ab5abe369fd2dd30e580</id><updated>2026-11-27T00:42:25Z</updated><published>2026-11-26T15:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-ig-metall-union-says-deal-reached-with-employers/a-80066792--f4aca602c9d5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-ig-metall-union-says-deal-reached-with-employers/a-80066792?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">IG Metall, representing millions of workers in Germany's metal and electrical industry, is the country's largest trade union. The deal came after more than 24 hours of talks with employers.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany: 2 arrested, suspected of plotting synagogue attack</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b75c71fd02432212a4d7609644473f58440476e56df3a27d8a674f5499b120d7</id><updated>2026-11-27T00:42:58Z</updated><published>2026-11-26T09:37:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-2-arrested-suspected-of-plotting-synagogue-attack/a-80057715--3c7a6577a7d2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-2-arrested-suspected-of-plotting-synagogue-attack/a-80057715?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Federal prosecutors say they have ordered the arrest of two members of a pro-Iranian group on suspicion of planning an attack on a synagogue. They were detained in the cities of Heidelberg and Cologne.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: 'We can no longer afford everything,' Merz says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bd27c163b4b3688f05d497d7f9c26076e97f8cb891ee004ba12dc0ad61a3805a</id><updated>2026-11-27T00:41:04Z</updated><published>2026-11-25T08:35:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-we-can-no-longer-afford-everything-merz-says/live-80042795--0bc2dba71ae9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-we-can-no-longer-afford-everything-merz-says/live-80042795?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The German chancellor has warned tax revenue means a tighter budget for 2027 and beyond. Meanwhile, President Steinmeier is in Kenya for the final leg of his Africa tour.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Freigang banned — Germany star to miss 2027 World Cup</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2ad2fd606f410f6b000675b64059d3fd7fda09b5837a5377cfe2572dfa6f07df</id><updated>2026-11-27T00:42:37Z</updated><published>2026-11-26T14:50:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/freigang-banned-germany-star-to-miss-2027-world-cup/a-80063930--642807df4daf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/freigang-banned-germany-star-to-miss-2027-world-cup/a-80063930?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany forward Laura Freigang has been suspended until October 2027 after missing three doping tests, ruling her out of next year's Women's World Cup in Brazil. Freigang has denied any intention to evade controls.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Joshua Kimmich critcizes Bayern bosses over Musiala health comments</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b140bdc63847fc614529722e2bd5aec5c1b2b17d6b5706be7644aa53465d8191</id><updated>2026-11-27T00:42:46Z</updated><published>2026-11-26T12:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/joshua-kimmich-critcizes-bayern-bosses-over-musiala-health-comments/a-80060155--f8755c2422c2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/joshua-kimmich-critcizes-bayern-bosses-over-musiala-health-comments/a-80060155?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Joshua Kimmich has slammed Bayern Munich's leadership over comments about Jamal Musiala's health issues. The bosses have questioned whether the player can return to previous form – and is still worth his high salary.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>€561 Billion and Still Not Enough: Germany's 2027 Budget Exposes a Coalition on the Brink</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fae5191bed023282f793218a266279ffa829f6eb0daf78be8ee6ec4b06fee2ed</id><updated>2026-11-27T00:41:04Z</updated><published>2026-11-25T16:06:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/561-billion-and-still-not-enough-germany-s-2027-budget-exposes-a-coalition-on-the-brink/a-80052664--c8b0f8b87743.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/€561-billion-and-still-not-enough-germany-s-2027-budget-exposes-a-coalition-on-the-brink/a-80052664?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The budget for 2027 has reached new highs, and pension funds, defense spending and a weak economy are increasing the pressure. At the same time, tensions are mounting within the government.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>German firms eye Africa as global trade shocks hit traditional markets</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4488107a1128b2a9a94e5c83bf1f202781382f7b62f60a1c9d531670c15884e6</id><updated>2026-11-27T00:41:04Z</updated><published>2026-11-25T14:38:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/german-firms-eye-africa-as-global-trade-shocks-hit-traditional-markets/a-80047671--b64160bb0ab9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/german-firms-eye-africa-as-global-trade-shocks-hit-traditional-markets/a-80047671?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">German businesses are optimistic about Africa, but Berlin's cautious approach to risk is holding them back from cashing in on the opportunities that their competitors from countries like the UAE and Turkey are seizing.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Ice hockey prospect Max Calce follows Leon Draisaitl's path, leaving Mannheim for Canada</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:31c976874cd6aad0f0339a4e6271fa2ad6363fd9e1b31b17f3627fe5682e9216</id><updated>2026-11-27T00:41:04Z</updated><published>2026-11-25T13:28:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ice-hockey-prospect-max-calce-follows-leon-draisaitl-s-path-leaving-mannheim-for-canada/a-80049458--4ca1ab8cf6e4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ice-hockey-prospect-max-calce-follows-leon-draisaitl-s-path-leaving-mannheim-for-canada/a-80049458?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The player widely seen as Germany's biggest ice hockey talent to come along in years is leaving the country's top professional league for Canada – changing tracks in his bid to make it to the NHL.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Has the 'Parthenon puzzle' been solved? The long quest to reassemble lost eastern pediment</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9f6dcac703ee114ca2c514fd6c279d73bdb58614773c4b69b94d89e123100b74</id><updated>2026-11-27T00:41:04Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T20:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/has-the-parthenon-puzzle-been-solved-the-long-quest-to-reassemble-lost-eastern-pediment/a-79982098--4f23b2ccbfc4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/has-the-parthenon-puzzle-been-solved-the-long-quest-to-reassemble-lost-eastern-pediment/a-79982098?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The depiction of the birth of the goddess Athena above the Parthenon's entrance is considered a masterpiece of ancient art. Now, a German research team has pieced together all the surviving fragments.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Wael Mohya could make German football history at 17</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:be802f4fbe22400806003fdff8c383adf8ff7b793e01664687487bfe0ae129a9</id><updated>2026-11-27T00:41:04Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T15:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/wael-mohya-could-make-german-football-history-at-17/a-79919787--677b2c671ea6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/wael-mohya-could-make-german-football-history-at-17/a-79919787?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">At just 17, Gladbach forward Wael Mohya has earned his first Germany call-up. The dual-national talent has chosen the DFB path for now — and could soon make modern national-team history.</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
